  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Timothy",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Counsel is given to teach true doctrine only—Christ came to save repentant sinners.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the commandment of God our Saviour, and Lord Jesus Christ, which is our hope;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto Timothy, my own son in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God our Father and Jesus Christ our Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Acts 16:1 (1–4); 1 Cor. 4:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "GR a true son according to."
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR lawful, true."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As I besought thee to abide still at Ephesus, when I went into Macedonia, that thou mightest charge some that they teach no other doctrine,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:3 (3–5); 3 Ne. 11:40."
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 129,
            "text": "Gal. 1:8 (6–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither give heed to fables and endless genealogies, which minister questions, rather than godly edifying which is in faith: so do.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Titus 1:14; 2 Pet. 1:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "GR offer, present."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "TG Edification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 131
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the end of the commandment is charity out of a pure heart, and of a good conscience, and of faith unfeigned:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Gal. 5:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Charity."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "2 Tim. 2:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "From which some having swerved have turned aside unto vain jangling;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "GR missed the mark."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "GR vain, idle, fruitless discussion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Desiring to be teachers of the law; understanding neither what they say, nor whereof they affirm.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "GR strongly assert."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But we know that the law is good, if a man use it lawfully;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing this, that the law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient, for the ungodly and for sinners, for unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Law of Moses."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Godliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "Gal. 3:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For whoremongers, for them that defile themselves with mankind, for menstealers, for liars, for perjured persons, and if there be any other thing that is contrary to sound doctrine;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Whore."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "GR homosexuals."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Homosexual Behavior."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "GR kidnappers."
          },
          {
            "start": 172,
            "end": 180,
            "text": "2 Tim. 4:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "According to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Trustworthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who hath enabled me, for that he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Philip. 4:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who was before a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and injurious: but I obtained mercy, because I did it ignorantly in unbelief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Acts 26:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Acts 8:3; 22:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "GR violent."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "1 Cor. 7:25."
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "John 9:39 (39–41). TG Ignorance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 100
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This is a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "1 Tim. 3:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "Matt. 9:13 (12–13). TG Jesus Christ, Atonement through."
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "Luke 5:32; John 9:39 (39–41)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Howbeit for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might shew forth all longsuffering, for a pattern to them which should hereafter believe on him to life everlasting.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG God, Mercy of."
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "TG Forbear."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "TG Example."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now unto the King eternal, immortal, invisible, the only wise God, be honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:15 (15–16)."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG God, Eternal Nature of; Immortality."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This charge I commit unto thee, son Timothy, according to the prophecies which went before on thee, that thou by them mightest war a good warfare;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "1 Tim. 4:14 (14–16); 2 Tim. 1:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Holding faith, and a good conscience; which some having put away concerning faith have made shipwreck:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "1 Ne. 15:24; D&C 6:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 101,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Individuals; Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Of whom is Hymenæus and Alexander; whom I have delivered unto Satan, that they may learn not to blaspheme.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "2 Tim. 2:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Acts 19:33 (33–34)."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "1 Cor. 5:5; D&C 78:12; 104:10 (9–10); 132:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
